WEBVTT

00:00:25.486 --> 00:00:29.466
RECORD OF LODOSS WAR
Chronicles of the Heroic Knight

00:00:29.490 --> 00:00:33.324
RECORD OF LODOSS WAR
Chronicles of the Heroic Knight

00:01:45.800 --> 00:01:49.896
Lodoss has now been divided
into three major pieces.

00:01:49.970 --> 00:01:52.302
The Alanian-Marmo alliance.

00:01:52.373 --> 00:01:55.900
The Lodoss Federation of Valis
and Flaim, which opposes them.

00:01:55.976 --> 00:01:57.466
And the kingdom of Moss,

00:01:57.545 --> 00:02:00.071
which continues to
be wracked by civil war.

00:02:00.147 --> 00:02:03.742
The civil war in Moss is
moving towards a conclusion.

00:02:11.225 --> 00:02:13.819
Due to the activity of the dragon
riders known as the Dragon Eyes...

00:02:13.894 --> 00:02:17.455
...under the command of Duke Redrick
of the Duchy of Highland and...

00:02:18.566 --> 00:02:21.558
...Queen Shirts, the reunification
of Moss is only a matter of time.

00:02:23.537 --> 00:02:26.234
At the same time, in Novice
in the kingdom of Alania...

00:02:26.307 --> 00:02:28.401
...the forces of Flaim
under King Kashue...

00:02:28.476 --> 00:02:31.502
...were engaging the Alanian forces
under the command of Duke Raster.

00:02:36.984 --> 00:02:38.884
The war has begun.

00:03:08.315 --> 00:03:10.545
Look! Our Alanian troops
are overwhelming...

00:03:10.618 --> 00:03:13.747
...the Flaim forces, said to
be the strongest in Lodoss!

00:03:14.188 --> 00:03:18.250
It's because we knew Prince Robess
was asking Flaim for reinforcements.

00:03:18.325 --> 00:03:22.057
Kashue's attack
was easy to predict.

00:03:22.129 --> 00:03:24.393
It looks like launching a
sneak attack after making...

00:03:24.465 --> 00:03:26.559
...our preparations
was the correct decision.

00:03:31.906 --> 00:03:35.035
Once I defeat Kashue and
take Flaim as my own...

00:03:35.109 --> 00:03:38.135
...it'll just be a matter of time
before I rule all of Lodoss!

00:03:38.813 --> 00:03:40.110
How could this have happened?!

00:03:40.181 --> 00:03:42.081
F- Forgive me, Your Highness!

00:03:42.149 --> 00:03:45.779
This attack force was made
up of mostly young knights.

00:03:45.853 --> 00:03:47.685
Most had never
been in battle before...

00:03:47.755 --> 00:03:49.245
They were so hungry for glory...

00:03:49.323 --> 00:03:53.624
...that they were caught by
the more experienced enemy.

00:03:53.694 --> 00:03:55.788
With the results being obvious.

00:03:55.863 --> 00:03:58.730
At this rate, we're only
strengthening the enemy!

00:03:58.799 --> 00:04:00.995
Move our mercenary division
up to engage their front line.

00:04:01.068 --> 00:04:04.834
In the meantime, we'll hit their
main forces being held in the rear!

00:04:04.905 --> 00:04:07.499
Are you going after the
duke yourself, Highness?

00:04:07.575 --> 00:04:10.510
I'm going to take Raster's head!

00:04:10.578 --> 00:04:14.811
Now show our overconfident enemies
how terrifying mercenaries can be!

00:04:15.282 --> 00:04:17.011
You took the words
out of my mouth, sir.

00:04:29.396 --> 00:04:30.522
Charge!

00:04:34.635 --> 00:04:36.694
A report, sir!

00:04:37.071 --> 00:04:40.439
Kashue has taken to the battlefield
and is coming this way!

00:04:40.508 --> 00:04:42.101
What?!

00:04:45.312 --> 00:04:46.905
Duke Raster!

00:04:46.981 --> 00:04:49.746
The man's a fool to attack
with such a small force!

00:04:53.654 --> 00:04:56.316
A reward for the one
who brings him down!

00:05:13.807 --> 00:05:15.241
FIRE!!

00:05:20.414 --> 00:05:22.940
That man...
Isn't he afraid of death?!

00:05:23.017 --> 00:05:27.181
Dammit, out of my way!
Kashue's head is mine!

00:05:30.824 --> 00:05:32.553
Kashue! Prepare to die!

00:05:41.468 --> 00:05:43.766
He... He jumped it?!

00:05:48.742 --> 00:05:52.337
King Kashue Arnague
of Flaim has arrived!

00:06:12.766 --> 00:06:14.427
He's...so strong!

00:06:22.977 --> 00:06:25.071
He's so strong! It's too much!

00:06:25.145 --> 00:06:27.307
What should we do, Duke Raster?!

00:06:33.520 --> 00:06:35.818
Now! Get going!

00:06:44.531 --> 00:06:50.698
With Raster having fled, the Alanian
forces were no match for Flaim's.

00:06:50.771 --> 00:06:55.106
Raster fled with his remaining
forces back to his capital, Alan...

00:06:55.175 --> 00:06:58.907
...and, using the general population
as a shield, settled in for a siege.

00:06:58.979 --> 00:07:02.643
In response, the Flaim forces have
completely surrounded Alan and...

00:07:02.716 --> 00:07:06.949
...Kashue has dispatched a messenger
offering Raster terms of surrender.

00:07:14.094 --> 00:07:16.756
It's taking too long! How long do
they intend to make us wait?!

00:07:16.830 --> 00:07:21.961
The negotiations are still going on.
All we can do is wait.

00:07:23.704 --> 00:07:25.672
Highness, he's back!

00:07:25.739 --> 00:07:27.901
Right! Bring him in!

00:07:34.214 --> 00:07:36.012
I'm back, Your Highness.

00:07:36.083 --> 00:07:40.020
| take it the negotiations
aren't going well.

00:07:40.454 --> 00:07:43.219
No, sir. He keeps repeating
that they'll only surrender-...

00:07:43.290 --> 00:07:45.884
...if we return to Flaim.

00:07:45.959 --> 00:07:48.929
If we do that, it's not
a surrender at all, is it?

00:07:48.996 --> 00:07:50.691
Looks like this
is going to drag on.

00:07:54.034 --> 00:07:59.165
Damn you, Raster! We have to
get to Marmo as soon as we can!

00:08:11.652 --> 00:08:14.053
Garrack, could you
just calm down a little?

00:08:15.622 --> 00:08:18.319
He's late. He's late!
He's late! He's late!

00:08:19.727 --> 00:08:21.388
The guy's hopeless...

00:08:23.630 --> 00:08:26.292
Well, Spark is sort of
late getting back here.

00:08:26.366 --> 00:08:28.596
The banquet's gonna start soon.

00:08:28.669 --> 00:08:31.832
If he isn't back in time for it...

00:08:32.272 --> 00:08:35.503
You don't suppose those
Valis sailors caught him, do you?

00:08:38.645 --> 00:08:40.204
They couldn't have!

00:08:42.916 --> 00:08:44.816
Spark!

00:08:44.885 --> 00:08:46.785
Are you hurt?!

00:08:47.488 --> 00:08:49.183
No... I'm fine...

00:08:49.256 --> 00:08:50.985
Yeah, he looks okay.

00:08:51.058 --> 00:08:53.117
We were worried about you!

00:08:53.193 --> 00:08:56.652
Really! Garrack kept
pacing around the room.

00:08:56.730 --> 00:08:58.994
We couldn't calm
him down for anything!

00:08:59.066 --> 00:09:02.036
He doesn't have
to hear about that!

00:09:02.102 --> 00:09:05.003
Anyway, I'm just relieved
you made it back in time.

00:09:05.072 --> 00:09:07.234
We thought you were
going to miss the banquet...

00:09:07.307 --> 00:09:09.708
...and we were
about ready to panic.

00:09:10.110 --> 00:09:12.078
Everyone, I'm sorry.

00:09:12.146 --> 00:09:14.774
Did something happen?

00:09:14.848 --> 00:09:18.978
Listen to me, all of you.
After what happened, I met a man.

00:09:23.390 --> 00:09:27.156
My name's Jay.
If you feel like it...

00:09:27.227 --> 00:09:30.197
...then come by the bridge
with your friends...

00:09:30.264 --> 00:09:31.629
after the moon rises tonight.

00:09:32.032 --> 00:09:34.558
| can take you to Kanon.

00:09:36.003 --> 00:09:37.767
And let you become
Marmo mercenaries,

00:09:37.838 --> 00:09:40.170
just like you want to be.

00:09:40.274 --> 00:09:41.503
Tonight?

00:09:41.842 --> 00:09:44.675
Yeah, tonight. Tomorrow's too late.

00:09:44.745 --> 00:09:47.407
I'll be waiting for you...friend.

00:09:54.388 --> 00:09:56.720
Is he really a Marmo?

00:09:57.891 --> 00:09:59.825
I think there's no question
about it.

00:09:59.893 --> 00:10:02.794
If a Marmo came here on a ship...

00:10:02.863 --> 00:10:05.833
...it means that ship is
a Marmo military vessel.

00:10:05.899 --> 00:10:08.698
It must be posing as a free trader.

00:10:08.769 --> 00:10:10.100
For what purpose?

00:10:10.170 --> 00:10:12.730
To transport their man
who's carrying...

00:10:12.806 --> 00:10:14.672
...the Soul Crystal Ball, of course.

00:10:14.741 --> 00:10:16.004
Yeah, you're right.

00:10:16.076 --> 00:10:20.570
When you think about it, this is
the clue we've been looking for.

00:10:22.049 --> 00:10:25.212
A military ship just for that?
No, I don't buy it.

00:10:25.285 --> 00:10:27.379
You think there's some
other reason for it?

00:10:27.454 --> 00:10:29.855
You only use a
military ship for one thing.

00:10:30.490 --> 00:10:33.323
They're planning to attack Valis!

00:10:36.096 --> 00:10:38.622
Huh?! There's no
way they would!

00:10:38.699 --> 00:10:41.691
You don't think they're going
after the temple of Falis, do you?!

00:10:41.768 --> 00:10:44.237
They're going after the second key
for resurrecting the Destroyer...

00:10:44.304 --> 00:10:46.671
...that's stored in the temple.
The Staff of Life!

00:10:46.740 --> 00:10:49.334
| think I agree with you!

00:10:49.409 --> 00:10:51.400
We'd better tell the king, fast!

00:10:51.478 --> 00:10:53.037
Spark!

00:10:53.113 --> 00:10:56.674
But if we tell King Etoh
this information...

00:10:56.750 --> 00:11:00.618
...he'll know we were poking
around inside of Valis!

00:11:01.054 --> 00:11:06.584
Besides, the Marmo attacking
is only a possibility.

00:11:06.660 --> 00:11:09.857
If we're wrong about this...

00:11:11.198 --> 00:11:14.099
Yeah, that's true, but...

00:11:19.106 --> 00:11:21.234
What's going on, everyone?

00:11:22.943 --> 00:11:27.881
...and as I said, this is all
just conjecture on our part.

00:11:27.948 --> 00:11:30.178
The guy did say he just
wants to take mercenaries...

00:11:30.250 --> 00:11:34.653
...who want to work for
the Marmo over to Kanon.

00:11:35.956 --> 00:11:40.416
But this theory about a
Marmo attack might be true.

00:11:40.494 --> 00:11:43.589
Shouldn't we tell
His Highness about this?

00:11:43.664 --> 00:11:46.326
That's what I said, but...

00:11:48.568 --> 00:11:51.503
And now the captain's like that.
| just don't get it.

00:11:51.571 --> 00:11:54.438
Why's he so torn up about this?

00:11:57.945 --> 00:11:59.811
Um, excuse me...

00:12:03.483 --> 00:12:05.508
C- Captain...?

00:12:08.855 --> 00:12:11.085
Gotta exercise.
I'll be right back.

00:12:18.932 --> 00:12:21.594
He's lost his way.

00:12:21.902 --> 00:12:23.700
Lost his way?

00:12:23.770 --> 00:12:26.899
No, maybe that's
not the best way to put it.

00:12:26.974 --> 00:12:28.965
It's more along the lines of...

00:12:29.042 --> 00:12:32.376
...he no longer knows
what he has to do.

00:12:32.446 --> 00:12:33.914
What he has to do?

00:12:33.981 --> 00:12:38.851
King Kashue's ORDERED us to stop
looking for the Soul Crystal Ball...

00:12:38.919 --> 00:12:41.354
...and go back to Flaim.

00:12:41.421 --> 00:12:42.149
Yeah...

00:12:42.222 --> 00:12:46.455
Meaning what we did in the port
of Roid violated those orders.

00:12:46.526 --> 00:12:49.621
But those orders came
from King Kashue!

00:12:49.696 --> 00:12:51.994
King Etoh had nothing
to do with them, right?!

00:12:52.065 --> 00:12:53.464
Think about what we did.

00:12:53.533 --> 00:12:57.094
We're foreign knights messing around
like we're in our own kingdom!

00:12:57.170 --> 00:13:00.140
Spark is afraid that what he
did may have put cracks...

00:13:00.207 --> 00:13:03.507
...into the alliance
between Flaim and Valis.

00:13:03.577 --> 00:13:07.036
And if Flaim and
Valis break ranks now...

00:13:07.114 --> 00:13:10.573
...they wouldn't be able to beat
the Marmo-Alanian alliance.

00:13:10.650 --> 00:13:14.245
And he didn't get any hard evidence
to prove the Marmo will attack.

00:13:14.321 --> 00:13:17.188
I'll bet he feels like an
idiot for not doing that.

00:13:17.257 --> 00:13:19.351
I get you...
There's a lot of things...

00:13:19.426 --> 00:13:22.054
...that go into becoming
a knight, aren't there?

00:13:22.129 --> 00:13:24.860
It's not like being
a mercenary at all.

00:13:38.979 --> 00:13:41.539
This is no time to be
going to any banquets.

00:13:41.615 --> 00:13:45.574
All we can do now is wait.
Until Spark makes his decision.

00:13:45.986 --> 00:13:49.081
A decision as a knight...huh?

00:13:49.756 --> 00:13:52.020
As a knight...

00:13:58.365 --> 00:14:00.993
Spark...
Shouldn't you rest a little?

00:14:06.606 --> 00:14:08.301
Swinging your sword
around when you're confused...

00:14:08.375 --> 00:14:10.901
...isn't exactly training, is it?

00:14:13.814 --> 00:14:17.409
Try to think about what's
most important instead.

00:14:22.622 --> 00:14:25.887
Do that, and I'm sure the
answer will come to you.

00:14:25.959 --> 00:14:27.449
I am thinking!

00:14:27.527 --> 00:14:30.394
I keep thinking, but I still
can't find the answer!

00:14:31.832 --> 00:14:33.027
People's lives...

00:14:33.100 --> 00:14:38.163
No, the entire future of
Lodoss may be riding on this.

00:14:38.238 --> 00:14:39.899
I KNOW that!

00:14:39.973 --> 00:14:44.410
But if we make the wrong
choice, Flaim and Valis might...

00:14:44.478 --> 00:14:47.175
That doesn't really matter
in the long run, does it?

00:14:48.715 --> 00:14:51.741
Neese! You're a cleric, which means
you just have to think about...

00:14:51.818 --> 00:14:56.016
...your order's teachings and how
things affect it! But I have to...

00:14:57.524 --> 00:15:02.086
I'm a knight! I have to think
about my duty to my kingdom!

00:15:04.998 --> 00:15:08.525
| see... Then I'll say nothing.

00:15:08.602 --> 00:15:11.264
You're free to do as you see fit.

00:15:19.412 --> 00:15:22.143
Dammit! Why does she have to be
so cheerfully simple all the time?!

00:15:22.215 --> 00:15:25.378
Doesn't she understand
human feelings?!

00:15:27.988 --> 00:15:30.423
Everyone, the banquet
is about to begin.

00:15:30.490 --> 00:15:32.549
Would you please
come to the great hall?

00:15:34.227 --> 00:15:36.093
We're out of time.

00:15:37.998 --> 00:15:38.897
Spark...

00:15:38.965 --> 00:15:41.127
Well, we have to go.

00:15:42.569 --> 00:15:46.267
We don't want King Etoh
to be suspicious of us.

00:15:49.743 --> 00:15:51.711
Wasn't Lady Neese with you?

00:15:52.245 --> 00:15:54.509
| thought she came
back in a few minutes ago.

00:15:54.581 --> 00:15:56.140
She didn't come back in here.

00:15:56.216 --> 00:15:58.150
Great! Not only do we have...

00:15:58.218 --> 00:16:00.209
...this banquet to deal with,
but now Neese has...!

00:16:00.287 --> 00:16:01.948
| wonder where she went.

00:16:02.022 --> 00:16:05.959
Y- You don't think Lady Neese went
to the temple of Falis, do you?!

00:16:08.161 --> 00:16:09.993
But why would she...?

00:16:10.063 --> 00:16:13.829
Have you forgotten?! The reason
Lady Neese came to Valis?!

00:16:13.900 --> 00:16:17.803
The Staff of Life,
the second key, is there!

00:16:18.438 --> 00:16:22.500
Is she planning to protect
it from the Marmo...?!

00:16:22.576 --> 00:16:26.069
And she went by herself?!
That's insane!

00:16:26.146 --> 00:16:30.947
If they steal the Staff of Life,
they'll come after her next!

00:16:31.017 --> 00:16:33.782
Where's the sense of putting
herself in that kind of danger?!

00:16:34.487 --> 00:16:38.651
It was because she knew
that Lady Neese went!

00:16:38.725 --> 00:16:42.127
To fight against her cursed
destiny of being the Doorway!

00:16:42.462 --> 00:16:44.328
That's right... Neese...

00:16:48.401 --> 00:16:50.369
She's been fighting all along!

00:16:50.437 --> 00:16:54.396
Fighting to stop the Destroyer's
resurrection all by herself!

00:16:54.841 --> 00:16:58.709
Try to think about what's
most important instead.

00:16:59.746 --> 00:17:03.683
Do that, and I'm sure the
answer will come to you.

00:17:03.750 --> 00:17:06.685
And despite that...
Despite that, I...!

00:17:07.220 --> 00:17:08.654
Neese!

00:17:09.923 --> 00:17:12.085
His Highness is in
the great hall, right?!

00:17:12.158 --> 00:17:13.557
Y- Yes, sir.

00:17:16.162 --> 00:17:20.861
It looks like he now
knows what he needs to do.

00:17:20.934 --> 00:17:24.029
| wonder what King Kashue
will say when hears about this.

00:17:24.104 --> 00:17:25.435
He'd probably be happy.

00:17:27.707 --> 00:17:29.732
What am I so confused about?!

00:17:29.809 --> 00:17:32.437
I've been so concerned
about duty and politics...

00:17:32.512 --> 00:17:35.538
...that I forgot about
what's most important!

00:17:38.418 --> 00:17:44.084
Didn't I swear I'd protect Neese?!
But despite that, I...!

00:17:44.791 --> 00:17:48.694
What's most important now is to
protect Neese and the Staff of Life!

00:17:48.762 --> 00:17:50.924
To stop the Destroyer
from being reborn!

00:17:54.901 --> 00:17:57.131
Hey! Who are you?!

00:18:00.240 --> 00:18:01.537
Forgive my rudeness, Your Highness!

00:18:01.608 --> 00:18:05.306
I've come because there's
something I must tell you!

00:18:05.378 --> 00:18:09.611
From the way you're acting,
| assume that dinner is off.

00:18:09.916 --> 00:18:11.077
Yes, sir!

00:18:11.918 --> 00:18:12.783
Garrack! Let's go!

00:18:12.852 --> 00:18:13.910
Right!

00:18:20.627 --> 00:18:23.824
| understand.
We'd better act at once.

00:18:23.897 --> 00:18:28.061
You believe him, Your Highness?!
He could be a Marmo spy!

00:18:28.368 --> 00:18:31.929
If I'm wrong, then lock me up in
prison or wherever you want to!

00:18:32.005 --> 00:18:33.063
Highness!

00:18:33.139 --> 00:18:35.107
We have areport from
our lookout towers!

00:18:35.175 --> 00:18:38.577
Flames have been spotted in the
direction of the temple of Falis!

00:18:38.645 --> 00:18:39.578
What?!

00:18:46.052 --> 00:18:49.852
And now Valis, too, is swept away
in the wave of war's chaos...

00:18:51.124 --> 00:18:52.148
Neese!

00:18:59.499 --> 00:19:01.490
Neese, I'm coming!

00:19:03.103 --> 00:19:06.004
Captain, you forgot something!

00:19:09.409 --> 00:19:13.710
Go now! I'll join you soon
with my royal guard.

00:19:14.347 --> 00:19:17.681
Thank you, Highness!
Everyone, let's go!

00:19:24.324 --> 00:19:26.122
I have no doubts anymore!

00:19:26.192 --> 00:19:29.355
The Staff of Life and Neese...

00:19:30.397 --> 00:19:32.991
I swear I'll protect them both!

00:19:43.109 --> 00:19:45.407
Welcome to Lodoss Island!

00:19:45.478 --> 00:19:48.175
And now, what you've been waiting
for, the second part of the show!

00:20:04.764 --> 00:20:07.165
Here's how the plan will work.

00:20:07.233 --> 00:20:11.136
Once they fall into the hole,
Il of fer to release them...

00:20:11.204 --> 00:20:13.536
...in exchange for the cookies.

00:20:17.710 --> 00:20:20.475
Naturally, I won't
REALLY let them go.

00:20:21.014 --> 00:20:24.416
| call it Operation Fall in the
Hole and Get the Cookies!

00:20:24.484 --> 00:20:25.781
Pow-Pow, Parn!

00:20:26.352 --> 00:20:28.446
Pow-Pow, Parn!

00:20:28.521 --> 00:20:31.456
You see? My name
just isn't funny like that.

00:20:31.524 --> 00:20:32.650
Yeah...

00:20:38.398 --> 00:20:39.888
Huh? A monster?

00:20:39.966 --> 00:20:43.061
That's Little Gargoyle,
Mama Dragon's messenger.

00:20:45.772 --> 00:20:47.638
What have we here? Oh...?

00:20:49.142 --> 00:20:51.634
What? What?
What's it say?

00:20:55.381 --> 00:20:58.214
A letter from Mama Dragon!
I'll be taking this!

00:20:58.284 --> 00:21:00.116
Agh! The Dark EIf!

00:21:00.186 --> 00:21:04.054
It must contain vital information
on how to make the cookies!

00:21:05.658 --> 00:21:07.183
| could have just
stolen your cookies!

00:21:07.260 --> 00:21:09.957
Give us that letter
back, you idiot!

00:21:10.029 --> 00:21:11.861
No way, Jose!

00:21:11.931 --> 00:21:13.023
Come back here!

00:21:15.768 --> 00:21:19.295
Spark? Where'd you go?

00:21:19.372 --> 00:21:23.036
Spark! Where are you?! Spark!

00:21:24.844 --> 00:21:28.405
Neese? I'm down here!

00:21:30.049 --> 00:21:32.814
No use...
Now what do we do?

00:21:35.622 --> 00:21:36.919
To be continued!

00:22:59.005 --> 00:23:02.236
The Marmo forces have landed
in the holy kingdom of Valis.

00:23:02.308 --> 00:23:06.870
We race to the temple of Falis
in pursuit of the missing Neese.

00:23:06.946 --> 00:23:10.348
Is the Staff of Life safe?
What about Neese?!

00:23:10.750 --> 00:23:14.618
What I must protect
lies inside raging flames!

00:23:15.054 --> 00:23:18.183
Next time, on Record of Lodoss War -
Chronicles of the Heroic Knight:

00:23:18.257 --> 00:23:20.726
"Mission... The Path One Follows."
